From 98d7b9c325f4d0d06de530271755961cd8bce3f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:53:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(delegate): a subagent can end its turn waiting on a
 background job

A subagent with a job that runs for hours had to poll, quit with "resume
later", or hand duplicate watchers to its parent. process_manage handoff now
takes resume_on_exit=true: the process stays the subagent's, the subagent ends
its turn, and its unit stays open. It shows as "waiting" (with waiting_on) in
delegate_task list and subagent.list. When a watched process exits, the
subagent continues its conversation with the exit code and output tail; after
delegation.max_wait_hours (24) it is resumed with a timeout notice. The parent
gets one result, when the subagent really finishes.

Handing off the same command again returns the first watch, and a subagent
holds at most eight. A restart hands the waiting subagent to the next gateway
with its watches; it reattaches the processes and goes on waiting. The
subagent prompt and the background-process note say to end the turn waiting.
